# taf.ul.sbts.energy_saving

[![Documentation](https://docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/projects/taf-ul-sbts-energy_saving/badge/)][1]
[![Requirements](https://taf.wrgitlab-pages.int.net.nokia.com/miscellaneous/static-badges/requirements.svg)](requirements/base.txt)
[![build status](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.sbts.energy_saving/badges/main/pipeline.svg)][2]
[![coverage report](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.sbts.energy_saving/badges/main/coverage.svg)][2]
[![latest release](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.sbts.energy_saving/badges/main/release.svg)][3]

High-level library that simplifies enabling, disabling, and monitoring energy saving modes (4G/LTE and 5G/NR) on SBTS nodes in the TAF environment. It focuses on operating on an existing configuration — it does not commission from scratch — but helps manage states and create the basic and mandatory objects (e.g., PSGRP/NRPGRP) with safe delta execution.

## Key features

- SCF backup and loading (XML parsing, pattern-based object search)
- Automatic enabling of energy saving for 4G (PSGRP) and/or 5G (NRPGRP)
- Complete 4G+5G workflow with an attempt to enable 4G/5G coordination when possible
- Power group management: group recreation with recommended parameters, periods, and cell lists
- Generating and applying deltas (create/update/delete, parameter updates, complex list items)
- Checking and waiting for cell states (whether any/all are in "energySaving")
- Parameter validation and updates from SCF (supports validation and thresholds)

## Architecture (high level)

- Interface: `EnergySavingInterface` — a simple entry point that combines managers and workflows into a cohesive API
- Workflows: `EnergySetupWorkflow` — chains multiple steps (4G/5G/coordination) into safe procedures
- Core managers:
  - `EnergySavingContext` — stores the connection alias, provides access to `admin`, and lazily creates managers
  - `ConnectionManager` — manages the connection alias within calls (the `with_connection` decorator)
  - `SCFManager` — SCF backup/restore, parsing, and object/ID discovery via regexes
  - `DeltaManager` — creating/committing/rolling back deltas, appending MO/param/list changes
  - `ParameterManager` — parameter diffs and validated updates
- Objects:
  - `Cell` (+ `NRCELLManager`, `LNCELManager`) — work with cells (IDs, statuses, SCF-based filtering)
  - `PowerGroup` (+ `NRPGRPManager`, `PSGRPManager`) — energy saving group objects (period and cell lists, recommended params)
- Decorators: `with_connection` — ensures a connection alias is available and the correct context is used during calls

## Limitations and assumptions

- The library does not commission a node from scratch. It assumes a valid configuration and operates on it (SCF backup/restore, deltas, parameters, groups).
- MRBTS/NRBTS/LNBTS object discovery is based on regex patterns and returns the first match — in topologies with many elements consider more precise selection.
- Some functions assume that target objects exist in SCF. If they are missing, explicit errors/messages are recommended.
---

## Supported Python versions

Library should work properly with Python versions specified within `requires-python` option in [pyproject.toml](pyproject.toml).

## Installation

Generic library installation process is described in [TAF user guide][4].

